PART 1. WHAT WAS CHECKED AND HOW
======================================================================
Code read line by line, looking for ways a visitor, a customer or a script could get
more than they should:
  - every server action in src/actions/ (who may call it, what the browser can send)
  - every service in src/services/ (orders, chat, reviews, shipments, products,
    categories, availability, catalog, notifications)
  - the API route src/app/api/chat-images/[messageId]/route.ts
  - the auth setup src/lib/auth.ts (read only, not changed: owner's rule)
  - all admin pages and the admin layout, and the storefront pages that show private data
  - helpers: money, masking, email templates, after-login redirect, tracking codes

Tools:
  - Vitest unit tests. The database is never touched: repositories are replaced by fakes.
    The order tests use an in-memory fake transaction that behaves like the real
    compare-and-swap updates, so race conditions can be tested.
  - The access tests call the REAL server actions and the REAL requireRole/getCurrentUser
    code; only the session lookup is faked (guest, MEMBER, STAFF, ADMIN).
  - A live attack against the production build (npm run build + next start on port
    3100), for the critical finding. The owner's dev server (port 3000) was not touched.
  - No real data was changed. No test user, order or product was created in the database.

Test files (new):
  src/services/orders.test.ts        placing orders, prices, stock, payment, statuses, races
  src/services/reviews.test.ts       buyers only, rating rules, name masking, moderation
  src/services/shipments.test.ts     public tracking page masking, admin form validation
  src/services/products.test.ts      admin product form: prices, stock, images, variants
  src/services/availability.test.ts  response time and "away until" limits
  src/actions/access.test.ts         all 24 admin actions refuse guest/customer/staff
  src/test/access-rules.test.ts      every admin page and action keeps its access check
  src/lib/money.test.ts, mask.test.ts, after-login.test.ts, shipments.test.ts,
  src/lib/email-templates.test.ts
  (plus the chat tests from 2026-09-25: messages, crypto, image-type, MessageBubble, PaymentBar)

